{"id":"n-20261012-s441kz","category":"finance","display_title":"Amazon in Talks to Buy Decart","display_title_he":"אמזון במגעים לרכישת דקארט","short_summary":"Amazon is reportedly negotiating the acquisition of Israeli AI startup Decart for approximately $7 billion. The talks follow failed acquisition attempts by other tech giants.","english_level":"C1","words":437,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Walla","domain":"finance.walla.co.il","url":"https://finance.walla.co.il/item/3871795","title":"דיווח: אמזון במגעים לרכישת דקארט הישראלית בכ-7 מיליארד דולר","published_at":"2026-10-12T07:18:00.000Z"},{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001559141","title":"דיווח: אמזון במגעים לרכישת דקארט הישראלית בכ-7 מיליארד דולר","published_at":"2026-10-12T02:22:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-12T02:22:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-12T07:23:24.791Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["According to reports by the Wall Street Journal, technology giant Amazon is engaged in advanced discussions to acquire the Israeli artificial intelligence startup Decart for an estimated seven billion dollars. Sources familiar with the matter indicate that while negotiations are progressing and a deal could potentially be finalized soon, the agreement remains unfinalized, leaving room for the possibility that talks might falter or another prospective buyer could emerge. If successfully concluded at this reported valuation, the transaction would rank among the largest technology exits in Israeli history and stand as one of Amazon's most substantial recent corporate acquisitions.","This valuation represents a remarkable seventy-five percent surge compared to May, when the startup was valued at approximately four billion dollars. Decart, established in 2023 by brothers Dean and Orian Leitersdorf alongside Moshe Shalev, operates out of San Francisco and has raised more than four hundred million dollars from prominent venture capital funds, including Sequoia Capital, Benchmark, and Radical Ventures. The news of Amazon's interest follows closely on the heels of a collapsed deal with Anthropic, the developer of the Claude chatbot, which withdrew from a proposed six billion dollar acquisition after completing its due diligence. Before that negotiation, Decart's founders reportedly declined an acquisition offer from Nvidia, choosing instead to favor Anthropic's proposal which had been offered in shares due to expectations regarding a future public offering.","From a technical perspective, Decart develops core technology that enables artificial intelligence models to run efficiently while facilitating seamless switching between chips produced by different manufacturers. This capability is exceptionally sought after amid the intense global race for computing power and ongoing industry efforts to reduce reliance on Nvidia hardware. Furthermore, the startup builds advanced world models, named Lucy and Oasis, which generate interactive three dimensional environments and real time video cost effectively. The relationship between the two companies is already established, as Amazon's cloud computing division, AWS, granted Decart early access to its proprietary Trainium3 artificial intelligence chip in 2025, with Amazon having since become a strategic customer of the firm.","For Amazon, integrating Decart could significantly bolster its ongoing initiatives to promote alternatives to Nvidia chips and expand its internal artificial intelligence infrastructure. This potential purchase would join a series of major acquisitions by Amazon in recent years, which include the purchase of MGM film and television studios in 2022 for approximately six and a half billion dollars and the announced acquisition of satellite company Globalstar earlier this year for roughly eleven billion dollars. Nevertheless, because the current discussions have not yet matured into a binding agreement, industry observers note that there is no absolute certainty that the acquisition will ultimately materialize."],"facts":[{"fact":"Amazon is in advanced talks to acquire Israeli AI startup Decart for approximately $7 billion.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Decart was founded in 2023 by Dean Leitersdorf, Orian Leitersdorf, and Moshe Shalev, operating from San Francisco.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The potential $7 billion valuation marks a 75% increase from May, when Decart was valued at around $4 billion.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Anthropic recently withdrew from a $6 billion acquisition deal for Decart following due diligence.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Decart previously turned down an acquisition offer from Nvidia.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Decart has raised over $400 million from venture capital funds including Sequoia Capital, Benchmark, and Radical Ventures.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Decart's technology allows efficient running of AI models and easy switching between chips from different manufacturers.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Decart develops world models such as Lucy and Oasis, which generate interactive 3D environments and video in real time.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Amazon previously gave Decart early access to its Trainium3 AI chip in 2025 as part of an existing strategic partnership.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"According","lemma":"according","pos":"prep","he":"לפי","name":null},{"text":"reports","lemma":"report","pos":"noun","he":"דיווחים","name":null},{"text":"Wall Street Journal","lemma":"Wall Street Journal","pos":"proper noun","he":"וול סטריט ג'ורנל","name":"Wall Street Journal"},{"text":"technology","lemma":"technology","pos":"noun","he":"טכנולוגיה","name":null},{"text":"giant","lemma":"giant","pos":"noun","he":"ענקית","name":null},{"text":"Amazon","lemma":"Amazon","pos":"proper noun","he":"אמזון","name":"Amazon"},{"text":"engaged","lemma":"engage","pos":"adjective","he":"מנהלת / עוס